## Original Content
Investors see different risks threatening markets, but broadly agree that traders should diversify beyond recent winners.

## Summary
Six investors shared their views on the biggest risks facing markets, though they disagreed on which specific threats were most significant. Despite these differences, all six broadly agreed that traders should diversify beyond recent market winners rather than concentrating in assets that have performed well recently.

## Key Points
- Six investors identified varying market risks threatening current market conditions
- Investors did not agree on which specific risk poses the greatest threat
- Despite differing risk assessments, all six investors converged on one common strategy
- The agreed-upon strategy is for traders to diversify beyond recent market winners
- Concentration in recently successful assets is viewed as a vulnerability by these investors


